{title: When He was on the cross}
{x_theme: blood, grace-mercy, cross, heaven}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/When He was on the cross.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
He knew me yet He loved me
He whose glory makes the Heavens shine
I’m so unworthy of such mercy
When He was on the cross, I was on His mind

{comment: Verse 1}
I’m not on an ego trip, I’m nothing on my own.
I’ve made mistakes, I often slip, just common flesh and bones.
But I’ll prove someday just why I say I’m of a special kind
For when He was on the cross, I was on His mind.

{comment: Verse 2}
The look of love was on His face, Thornes were on His head.
The blood was on His scarlet robe, Stained a crimson red.
Though His eyes were on the crowd that day, He looked ahead in time.
For when He was on the cross, I was on His mind.
